00:00:00,240 --> 00:00:03,000
Welcome to the Intelligent Document
 
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:06,000
Processing Platform, by ZenLabs AI Foundry.
 
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:10,000
Every enterprise runs on documents,
 
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:13,500
contracts, claims, invoices, policies,
 
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:16,500
and regulatory filings, across banking,
 
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:19,500
insurance, healthcare, legal, and supply chain.
 
00:00:20,500 --> 00:00:23,500
Processed manually, this work is slow,
 
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:26,000
expensive, and error-prone.
 
00:00:26,500 --> 00:00:28,500
IDP changes that entirely.
 
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,500
One end-to-end pipeline, ingest any
 
00:00:32,500 --> 00:00:35,500
document, extract every field with a
 
00:00:35,500 --> 00:00:38,500
confidence score, validate against your
 
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:41,500
enterprise standards, and route exceptions
 
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:44,000
to a human-in-the-loop workbench.
 
00:00:45,500 --> 00:00:48,000
The dashboard is your command center,
 
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:51,000
eight live KPIs, a real-time pipeline
 
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:53,500
breakdown, and quick-access cards for
 
00:00:53,500 --> 00:00:55,500
every document type you process.
 
00:00:57,000 --> 00:00:58,500
Stage one, ingestion.
 
00:00:59,500 --> 00:01:02,500
Documents arrive via portal, FTP, email,
 
00:01:02,500 --> 00:01:05,500
or API, PDF, scanned, TIFF, Word, or XML,
 
00:01:05,500 --> 00:01:07,000
up to 50 megabytes.
 
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:10,500
The moment a document lands, the AI
 
00:01:10,500 --> 00:01:12,000
pipeline triggers automatically.
 
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:15,500
The inbox lets you search by party,
 
00:01:15,500 --> 00:01:18,500
filter by status, and check each
 
00:01:18,500 --> 00:01:21,000
document's readability score for OCR quality.
 
00:01:22,500 --> 00:01:24,500
Stage two, extraction. Every document
 
00:01:24,500 --> 00:01:27,000
flows through six automated steps.
 
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:31,000
OCR converts it to structured text. NLP
 
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:33,500
identifies structure. Classification
 
00:01:33,500 --> 00:01:36,000
determines document type and status.
 
00:01:36,500 --> 00:01:39,500
The large language model then extracts
 
00:01:39,500 --> 00:01:42,500
every material field, a clause, a claim
 
00:01:42,500 --> 00:01:45,500
line, an invoice item, or a regulatory data point.
 
00:01:46,500 --> 00:01:49,000
Stage three, validation against
 
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:51,500
enterprise standards. Each value is
 
00:01:51,500 --> 00:01:54,500
checked against your playbook, policies,
 
00:01:54,500 --> 00:01:57,000
master data, and business rules.
 
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:00,500
A field-level confidence score and final
 
00:02:00,500 --> 00:02:03,500
document score determine whether it clears
 
00:02:03,500 --> 00:02:05,500
automatically or routes for review.
 
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:09,000
Stage four, human-in-the-loop review.
 
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:12,500
The Workbench surfaces only the fields
 
00:02:12,500 --> 00:02:15,000
that fell below threshold, alongside the
 
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:17,500
exact source text. Analysts confirm,
 
00:02:17,500 --> 00:02:20,500
override, or reject, and every decision
 
00:02:20,500 --> 00:02:23,000
feeds back into the model. Accuracy
 
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:24,500
compounds over time.
 
00:02:25,500 --> 00:02:28,500
The pipeline refreshes every four seconds.
 
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:32,500
This same pipeline powers use cases
 
00:02:32,500 --> 00:02:35,500
across every industry. Let us walk through
 
00:02:35,500 --> 00:02:37,500
one in depth, capital markets.
 
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:41,500
Capital Markets teams process thousands
 
00:02:41,500 --> 00:02:44,500
of ISDA master agreements, credit support
 
00:02:44,500 --> 00:02:47,500
annexes, trade confirmations, and KYC
 
00:02:47,500 --> 00:02:50,500
bundles every year, each requiring precise
 
00:02:50,500 --> 00:02:53,000
extraction of elections and risk parameters.
 
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:56,500
The ISDA module has four tabs, Upload,
 
00:02:56,500 --> 00:02:59,000
Extraction, Review, and Deviations.
 
00:03:00,500 --> 00:03:03,000
On Extraction, elections from the schedule
 
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:06,000
are grouped by Category, Termination, Tax,
 
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:08,500
and Miscellaneous, each showing extracted
 
00:03:08,500 --> 00:03:11,500
value, source text, location, and confidence score.
 
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:15,500
The Review Workbench routes low-confidence
 
00:03:15,500 --> 00:03:18,000
fields to analysts beside the exact
 
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:20,500
source clause, human attention only
 
00:03:20,500 --> 00:03:21,500
where it is needed.
 
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:25,500
The Deviations tab compares every election
 
00:03:25,500 --> 00:03:28,000
against your firm's standard positions,
 
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:30,500
showing what agrees, what falls within
 
00:03:30,500 --> 00:03:33,000
tolerance, and what needs escalation,
 
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:36,000
with approval workflows for legal, treasury,
 
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:39,000
and credit risk. Export the full report as CSV.
 
00:03:40,500 --> 00:03:42,500
That is the full end-to-end workflow,
 
00:03:42,500 --> 00:03:45,500
ingestion, extraction, validation, and
 
00:03:45,500 --> 00:03:47,000
review, where it matters.
 
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:50,500
One pipeline, every industry, purpose-built
 
00:03:50,500 --> 00:03:52,500
modules for the documents that matter most.
 
00:03:53,500 --> 00:03:56,000
Faster processing, higher accuracy,
 
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:57,500
complete auditability.
 
